  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, with all 6 witnesses passing and 1 of the 6 runs used. I wrote the rule, the witnesses and `task_result.md`.\n\n**Rule**\n- **Who it covers:** any member of the vehicle aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle occupies a highway that has a median or divider on it.\n- **The duty:** if the vehicle occupies such a median or divider, either the median has an opening (a crossover) there, or the vehicle is also inside an intersection. The obligation repeats the full highway condition, because a region picked in the applicability can't be referred to from the obligation.\n- **Narrowings:** none of my own. The record's two readings, that a vehicle on the road counts as driven and that an opening or intersection being present counts as \"established by a public authority\", are kept as they are.\n\n**Witnesses** (car is track 1; highway region 10; medians 11, 13 and 14; intersection 12):\n\n| Scenario | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | crosses a median with no opening, no intersection | violated |\n| `permit` | drives on the right-hand roadway, never touches the median | compliant |\n| `idle` | undivided highway, crosses the centre line | not applicable |\n| `blind` | drives next to the median, `rel.occupies` masked | unknown |\n| `branch_1` | crosses at a median section with an opening | compliant |\n| `branch_2` | clips the median's nose while inside an intersection | compliant |\n\nThe node needed no correction, so the only thing to report back is the result itself.\n\nFiles are in `library/`:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o2.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o2.lean`\n- `task_result.md` (in the working directory)",
